Hi All, Please focus on the following topics. This week you will need have to complete the following
Vue.JS 

1. Architecture & Component Design

Single File Components (SFCs): Structuring <script setup>, <template>, and <style scoped> within .vue files.
Component Communication: Mastering parent-to-child data flow via props and child-to-parent notifications via emit.
Slots System: Implementing flexible layouts using default, named, and scoped slots for passing template content.
Provide / Inject: Passing dependency data deeply down a component tree without manually passing props through every layer.

⚡ 2. Advanced Reactivity (Composition API)

Ref vs. Reactive: Knowing when to use ref() (for primitives and deep object tracking) versus reactive() (exclusively for objects and reactive state constraints).
Computed & Watchers: Optimizing performance with cached computed() properties, and handling side effects via watch() and watchEffect().
Custom Composables: Extracting and sharing stateful logic across multiple components using standard naming conventions (e.g., useFetch).
Shallow Reactivity: Utilizing shallowRef() and shallowReactive() to optimize performance for large, immutable datasets.

🛠️ 3. Built-in Components & Templates

Dynamic Components: Swapping active UI layers dynamically on a page using the <component :is="..."> element.
KeepAlive: Caching component instances dynamically when switching between views to preserve user input or scroll state.
Teleport: Rendering a component's template node into a different part of the DOM tree (useful for modals, tooltips, and notifications).
Suspense: Managing loading states and fallback content for components wrapping asynchronous dependencies.

🚀 4. Ecosystem & Routing

Vue Router: Configuring client-side routing, nested routes, dynamic route matching, and programmatic navigation.
Navigation Guards: Securing specific application views using global, per-route, or in-component authentication checks.
Pinia State Management: Managing global, centralized application states with modular stores, actions, and getters.
Server-Side Rendering (SSR): Introducing frameworks like Nuxt.js to build SEO-friendly applications with hybrid rendering capabilities.

🔧 5. Tooling, Testing & Production

Vite Toolchain: Configuring the local build pipeline, environment variables, aliases, and asset optimization.
Testing: Writing isolated unit tests via Vitest / Vue Test Utils, and end-to-end integration tests using Cypress or Playwright.
TypeScript Integration: Implementing strict type safety for component properties, event payloads, and global state objects.
Performance Optimization: Leveraging lazy loading routes, component async chunks, and analyzing build footprints using visualizers.